    "b-sks-rc-entities-intro": {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "ENTITY \u2014 An "
        },
        {
          "insert": "entity",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is a curated knowledge subject the build report does not list: a source file, a struct, a struct field, a function parameter, a game concept, a developer pattern. Like "
        },
        {
          "insert": "target",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " it is pure identity \u2014 but where a target row is mechanical, an entity row is a decision. Everything debatable about an entity, including its human-readable name, is a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "fact",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " row on it: an "
        },
        {
          "insert": "inferred_name",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " fact is the display name; "
        },
        {
          "insert": "purpose",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "inferred_type",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " facts say what we think it is. The "
        },
        {
          "insert": "locator",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " pins which real thing the row is; "
        },
        {
          "insert": "link",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows join it to targets and to other entities; the knowledge-record view assembles its facts like any other subject's."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-sks-rc-entities-intro",
      "children": []
    },
    "b-sks-rc-entities-admission": {
      "type": "callout",
      "props": {
        "kind": "decision",
        "title": "Invariant \u2014 curated in, nothing operational out",
        "tone": "success"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "entity",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rows are written by the librarian, never by the report and never by reconciliation. Nothing operational hangs off one: no "
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker_run",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", no "
        },
        {
          "insert": "target_status",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", no ledger entries, never in the work queue, never counted in the target set. An entity exists to carry meaning; an entity nobody has facts for has no reason to exist."
        }
      ],
      "id": "b-sks-rc-entities-admission",
      "children": []
    },
